Title: BASEMENT TAPE
Author: Kevin Shaw
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. SUBURBAN HOUSE - FOYER - DAY

LEAH PARK unlocks her late father's house. Keys still on a fishhook by the door.
LEAH
One week to empty it. Then I never come back.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

Boxes everywhere. A VHS CAMCORDER and labeled tapes on a shelf.
LEAH
Last thing I need is home movies.

INT. BASEMENT - LATER

She plays CHRISTMAS '94. Family dinner. Laughter. Then a glitch.
ON TAPE — FATHER
Leah, don't rewind this one.

INT. KITCHEN - NIGHT

Leah makes tea upstairs. The basement TV glow spills under the door.
LEAH
I unplugged you.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

The camcorder still runs. Timestamp: 3:07 AM. The label reads CHRISTMAS '93. Her father watches the lens.
ON TAPE — FATHER
You were always down here.

INT. BASEMENT STAIRS - NIGHT

Footsteps creak overhead. Leah lives alone.
LEAH
Hello?

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

Behind Leah: a FLOOR TRAPDOOR she never noticed, slightly open.
LEAH
That wasn't here when I was twelve.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

On tape, her father points at the same trapdoor. Live and recorded align.
ON TAPE — FATHER
You forgot the rest of the house.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

Leah kneels by the trapdoor. Cold air exhales from below.
LEAH
Three weeks in this house, Dad, and the walls keep moving.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

She lifts the door. A child's night-light glows under the floor — her childhood bedroom, preserved, waiting.
LEAH
I never left. Not since I was eight. Did I?

FADE OUT.


THE END
